  "plan": {
    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "metadata": {
      "name": "BTC daily trend dip and rip",
      "assetClass": "CRYPTO",
      "timeframe": "1d",
      "createdBy": "IMPORTED",
      "direction": "BOTH",
      "description": "Found in real BTC/USD daily history from 2018 to October 2026 (chosen on 2018-2022, confirmed unchanged on 2023-2026). Trade with the trend, against the short-term extreme: while the daily close is above its 40-day average, buy when the 2-day RSI falls below 15 (a sharp dip); while it is below, sell short when the 2-day RSI rises above 85 (a sharp rally). Exit when the close crosses back over the 10-day average, at an 8% stop, or after 30 days. One position at a time, 95% of equity. The 40-day average decides the direction, so it buys dips in up-trends and sells rallies in down-trends by itself. Neighbouring settings (50- and 60-day average) were profitable in 7 of 9 years too; losing years were 2018 and 2024."
    },
